"""
D2C Email Performance Report — 2025 vs 2026
==============================================

Purpose: show whether sending MORE emails correlates with BETTER results
(opens) or just more unsubscribes, for Focus on Energy's D2C emails
(Packs, OLM, Homeboost combined — no category breakdown), plus a separate
tab digging into WHY people unsubscribed from the single highest-unsub
campaign in each year.

Run:
    pip install streamlit pandas numpy plotly
    python -m streamlit run d2c_email_report.py

By default the Email Performance tab loads "d2c-campaigns.csv" from the
same folder. The Unsubscribe Reasons tab has its own uploaders — those
per-contact exports are named after whichever campaign happens to have the
most unsubscribes that year, so there's no fixed filename to default to.

All rates are volume-weighted (total unsubs or opens across all included
campaigns ÷ total emails sent), not a simple average of each campaign's own
rate — so a 180,000-recipient send counts proportionally more than a
100-recipient test send, rather than every campaign counting equally
regardless of size.
"""

